</div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">Design, manufacture and supply</h2><figure><img src="/assets/img/2024/08/10/industrial_furniture_control_centers.jpg" alt="Ergonomic control center operator furniture" width="635" height="505" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>Ergonomic control center operator furniture</figcaption></figure>
<p>ISYSTEMS AUTOMATION designs, manufactures and supplies control room equipment and operator furniture. Clients include LUKOIL Energy and Gas, Dalkia Termo Prahova and Nuclearelectrica.</p>
<p>Delivery covers the control room as a working environment, not a furniture catalogue: layout and sightlines, acoustics, lighting and microclimate, power distribution and backup, auxiliary equipment, and the operator interface — console arrangement, screen placement and reach distances. The ergonomic basis is ISO 11064; the full design rationale is under <a href="/industries/control-centers.html">Control Centers</a>.</p></div></section><section class="section section--tint"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">What each delivery includes</h2><p><strong>Acoustics.</strong> Background noise and reverberation controlled so speech between operators and audible alarms both work in the same room.</p>
<p><strong>Layout.</strong> Sightlines to the overview display from every console position, circulation that does not cross behind a working operator, and maintenance access without entering the operating area.</p>
<p><strong>Lighting and microclimate.</strong> Illuminance and glare control for screen work, temperature and air distribution for equipment and operators on a continuous shift.</p>
<p><strong>Power supply.</strong> Distribution, backup and changeover for consoles, displays and the control system.</p>
<p><strong>Operator interface.</strong> Consoles, screen arrangement and controls decided with the control system — so alarm philosophy and HMI layout are not reconciled on site after the furniture is fixed.</p></div></section>
